# Plebian-OS 0.2.2 release environment.
#
# STATUS: coordinated source integration CANDIDATE; final human review pending.
# Required F101/F104 qualification and artifact acceptance remain open.
# Every component *_REF is a bare 40-character SHA. Before acceptance, publish
# the reviewed source commits without tags and verify fetching each exact SHA
# from its remote. PLEBIAN_OS_REF is the
# release tag by the recorded exception (see its comment). Where a pin moved
# since 0.2.1 the comment above it says from what, to what, and why; where it
# did not move the comment says "held". The same values, in the same order,
# are mirrored in the closure table of releases/0.2.2-notes.md, and
# tests/test_release_versioning.py refuses a mismatch between the two.
#
# What each advance bought is in CHANGELOG.md under [0.2.2]; the 0.2.1 -> 0.2.2
# transition an installed machine goes through is in UPGRADING.md. 0.2.1's own
# selection history stays in releases/0.2.1.env and is not repeated here.

PLEBIAN_OS_VERSION=0.2.2
PLEBIAN_OS_RELEASE_MODE=1

# F107-A: normal media ships no account or password, so the deprecated
# IMAGE_PASSWORD / RANDOM_PASSWORD keys are absent by requirement, not by
# oversight — remaster-iso.sh refuses this manifest if either is merely set.

# The release tag, which the owner creates at RELEASING.md "Cutting 0.2.2"
# step 4, after the closure commit it names. This is the one ref that is not a
# bare SHA, and the reason is structural: release mode requires this ref to
# resolve to the provisioner's own HEAD, and no commit can contain its own SHA,
# so only a tag created after the commit can close that loop. Release builds
# retain this local tag as metadata and write its resolved HEAD to firstboot.
# That exact commit must be fetchable remotely before building; the release
# tag can remain local until installation acceptance and final human review.
PLEBIAN_OS_REF=v0.2.2
PLEBIAN_OS_REPO=https://github.com/itsmygithubacct/plebian-os.git
PLEBIAN_OS_BRANCH=

# Advanced from 0.2.1's 6e1d3cc through the 0.2.2 clipboard-holder fixes to
# 5eb87bb5f80e0c469ab1f8d74f5fb64cb700f2ba, which adds the FluidSynth
# audio hold-off and related checks. The suite stops
# depending on the operator's ambient session and gets one environment
# sanitiser instead of four; and the session holds the X CLIPBOARD and PRIMARY
# selections through autocutsel so copied text outlives the app that copied it
# (PLEB_CLIPBOARD opts out). The two subsequent holder-detection fixes match
# the actual process command line and require the same DISPLAY, so repeated
# login reuses a holder without starving a nested display of its own.
# rc2: f80f357 merges pleb main (install libfluidsynth3 rather than the
# fluidsynth player; stop warning about pleb's own tb command). a697a36
# installs /usr/local/go readable by every user: the update's umask 077 had
# staged it mode 700, so non-root Go checks failed on any host below Go 1.26.
# 6d9f014 rolls Kilix and pleb back without recursing into submodules (a
# recursive checkout died part-way on an embedded submodule with linked
# worktrees) and accepts a command link that already reaches the right file.
# 7d4f2ca sets the microphone input to 45% on a user's first Pleb session
# (PLEB_MIC_DEFAULT; recorded once, so a later user choice is kept).
# 1ae3c18 bounds the owned desktop session's child lifetimes, defers signals
# until identities are published, and supervises kiosk/recovery terminals.
# d40d77a aligns the termination test with the session's bounded cleanup exit.
# fac8b18 isolates the release tests from a developer's live display and
# installed closure files without changing session runtime behavior.
# bb30f5b documents the indirect parent identity assignment for ShellCheck.
# RC5 hosted CI installs python3-tk and xrandr for the display-dialog tests (4c08e6a).
PLEB_REF=4c08e6aff6e8a0c216a5d8c4fc3bca1042d66236
PLEB_REPO=https://github.com/itsmygithubacct/pleb.git
PLEB_BRANCH=
# Advanced from 0.2.1's a4d1e0fb: VERSION and provider manifest
# 0.2.2 with a test that keeps them together; send-text allowed within one OS
# window on the unauthenticated path, with the window rule tested; two fixtures
# no longer race make's timestamps. Everything 0.2.1 gated — the Kitty 0.48.2
# engine and the CVE-2026-72913 fix that entered at 6e1f2de5 — is an ancestor
# of this commit. The provisioner asserts the built engine reports exactly
# '0.2.2'; the selected commit retains the coordinated version change.
# Advanced 2026-09-07 from 15ab485e by exactly one commit on it, which moves
# only the content-catalog gitlink (94ddbc75 -> 07431765) so the shared catalog
# offers kilix-techno at 0992edcb (F124, four review seats) and kilix-graphs at
# 720af007 (its no-clobber fix, re-reviewed). The catalog commit is the
# gitlink's own base plus those four entries; the catalog's main also advances
# the kilix-tui-utils package pin, deliberately not taken here. Seat ae0a42b2
# ACCEPT: 609/609 Kilix tests at both commits, both apps install and run
# through the launcher, no consumer of this pin needs it on main.
# The earlier integration candidate merged that catalog commit with the contained-app
# fixes at 8744097, then protects live legacy profiles and profiles whose
# owner start time cannot be read. It validates persistent-profile ancestors,
# preserves mouse gesture modifiers and diagnoses input/output independently.
# Two CI fixture corrections retain the same reviewed runtime behavior and
# content gitlink. Validation and the final independent review are recorded
# in releases/0.2.2-notes.md.
# Advanced from 62cb5760 to the integrated rc1 head, then from 30922e5e through
# 849ed10d to 3a257725 so catalog builds use a private temporary cache and
# remove group/other write permissions inherited through Git's caller umask,
