# Held from 0.2.1, for the reason 0.2.1 recorded once it had been measured:
# 4a331173 is HEAD and refs/heads/main of kilix-waydroid and the tree there IS
# the F121 application; F121 was deferred out of 0.2.1 and is not implemented
# for 0.2.2 either; and no provisioning path clones or installs this
# repository — every reference to it is closure validation, a release-mode
# canonicality check, or manifest/provenance recording. The OS half is pinned
# separately below as PLEBIAN_OS_INSTALL_WAYDROID / _WAYDROID_CLOSURE_SHA256.
#
# It stays because release mode puts KILIX_WAYDROID_REF in the required-refs
# loop and refuses a build without a canonical 40-character SHA. Removing it
# needs the F120 root list amended in the same change, which is an owner
# decision and has not been made. So a deferred stream's commit is still a
# hard precondition for a release build, and that is worth knowing rather than
# papering over.
KILIX_WAYDROID_REF=4a331173caf36b3235679715e153e4154b85651f
KILIX_WAYDROID_REPO=https://github.com/itsmygithubacct/kilix-waydroid.git
KILIX_WAYDROID_BRANCH=

