# Read-aloud closure, plus advertised first-use dictation and TTS pulls.
# KILIX_VOICE_REF advances from 06d1f672 through 25ec0917 to af9398e3:
# foreground TTS auditions, a provider reply benchmark, hardware-aware tier
# selection and first-use Piper/Qwen setup. The last commit exposes GPU fit
# before its lazy runtime install. The last commit adds the guarded Base GPU
# tier. The follow-up fixes Pocket worker-thread generation and adds its
# measured CPU tier and first-use refusal/recovery tests. Vosk URLs and
# digests remain held. The latest commit adds the explicit receipt-required
# Qwen provider client path without selecting it as the read-aloud default.
# The follow-up stops Pocket's worker threads before an interrupted reply
# returns, so the next reply no longer races them.
#
# OD-BB (OQ-C1) changed what these keys instruct, not what they name:
#   KILIX_VOICE_REF           the pinned kilix-voice source commit the image
#                             provisions. Source code; unchanged in meaning.
#   KILIX_VOICE_LIB_*         the Vosk wheel (vosk/libvosk.so, an Apache-2.0
#                             shared object — code, not weights). Now the
#                             authority a later first-use dictation install
#                             verifies the wheel against; firstboot fetches it
#                             no longer, because at KILIX_VOICE_REF the
#                             installer's dictation leg is all-or-nothing and
#                             that leg is what fetches the weights.
#   KILIX_VOICE_MODEL_URL     the upstream source of the speech model. The same
#   KILIX_VOICE_MODEL_SHA256  URL and archive digest kilix-content's
#                             vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15 asset record carries,
#                             and what the F100 carrier will attest. The image
#                             never fetches it; the user does, at first use,
#                             after being shown the licence and accepting.
#   PLEBIAN_OS_INSTALL_VOICE_MODEL=1
#                             "this release advertises a first-use pull of the
#                             dictation model". It is NOT an instruction to
#                             download or install weights. Provisioning always
#                             takes the read-aloud-only leg; see
#                             PROVISION_VOICE_WEIGHTS in
#                             provision/plebian-os-provision.sh.
# No pin became meaningless, so none is removed: each is still the authority
# something downstream reads.
# e3f1d6b adds the whisper engine (whisper-small-en, through the pinned
# kilix-whisper-stt provider) and `kilix stt --setup-default`.
# a12be47 reports a download that fails after the licence was accepted as
# failed, not declined, so Kilix 95 keeps offering dictation.
KILIX_VOICE_REF=a12be47e289ca03fccd46840276add1833df5760
KILIX_VOICE_LIB_VERSION=0.3.45
KILIX_VOICE_LIB_URL=https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/fc/ca/83398cfcd557360a3d7b2d732aee1c5f6999f68618d1645f38d53e14c9ff/vosk-0.3.45-py3-none-manylinux_2_12_x86_64.manylinux2010_x86_64.whl
KILIX_VOICE_LIB_SHA256=25e025093c4399d7278f543568ed8cc5460ac3a4bf48c23673ace1e25d26619f
KILIX_VOICE_MODEL_URL=https://alphacephei.com/vosk/models/vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15.zip
KILIX_VOICE_MODEL_SHA256=30f26242c4eb449f948e42cb302dd7a686cb29a3423a8367f99ff41780942498
PLEBIAN_OS_INSTALL_VOICE_MODEL=1
# The accepted F100 model compliance carrier (OD-BA, OD-BB, OD-BC) that lets
# this release advertise the speech models above. build/remaster-iso.sh
# refuses PLEBIAN_OS_INSTALL_VOICE_MODEL=1 unless it verifies: generated by
# build/generate-model-compliance.py, graded by two independent seats.
PLEBIAN_OS_VOICE_CARRIER_DIR=releases/0.2.2-model-compliance
PLEBIAN_OS_VOICE_CARRIER_SHA256=d81951166a4983757499cc21c09f44396e1fc13c9f97bba6816e6328b45c140d
PLEBIAN_OS_VOICE_CARRIER_RECEIPT_SHA256=007edb4dce597ad9147ef99dc92a77ac3d07e72c316f8af46691c22e89162e1b

# Hash-bound Waydroid first-use closure, from the requirements.
PLEBIAN_OS_INSTALL_WAYDROID=1
PLEBIAN_OS_WAYDROID_CLOSURE_SHA256=4ad7a4d44eef6ce4e90173491d0c6c8da02b3764d0d20d1df67ca7eeaa7e4175

# Native runtime package, built from the pinned EnCodec source and content.
# This content ref remains d9a1335d for the native-deb candidate; it is not
# Kilix's newer speech-catalog gitlink. rc2 replaces rc1's native-deb-rc1
# (exact Depends, byte-pinned system libraries) with native-deb-rc2 from
# e0655faa: Depends and the v2 record state the versions built against as
# minimums, because 0.2.2 machines take live Debian security updates and the
# exact pins refused the package on a patched libc6/OpenSSL. Two snapshot
# builds were byte-identical. F101 qualification remains open.
